  "atoms": [
    {
      "id": "a0",
      "pos": 1,
      "text": "Immanuel Kant's 1795 essay \"Perpetual Peace\" is cited as the intellectual origin of democratic peace theory.",
      "factual": true,
      "stance": "asserted"
    },
    {
      "id": "a1",
      "pos": 2,
      "text": "Michael Doyle revived the Kantian argument in a two-part 1983 article in Philosophy and Public Affairs.",
      "factual": true,
      "stance": "asserted"
    },
    {
      "id": "a2",
      "pos": 3,
      "text": "The normative explanation holds that democracies externalize domestic norms of peaceful conflict resolution into their foreign relations.",
      "factual": true,
      "stance": "asserted"
    },
    {
      "id": "a3",
      "pos": 4,
      "text": "Kant published \"Perpetual Peace\" in 1812.",
      "factual": false,
      "stance": "asserted"
    },
    {
      "id": "a4",
      "pos": 5,
      "text": "The institutional explanation holds that electoral accountability and legislative checks slow a leader's ability to mobilize for war.",
      "factual": true,
      "stance": "asserted"
    },
    {
      "id": "a5",
      "pos": 6,
      "text": "The two states in the crisis dyad shared liberal norms of peaceful conflict resolution.",
      "factual": true,
      "stance": "asserted"
    },
    {
      "id": "a6",
      "pos": 7,
      "text": "The leaders in the crisis dyad faced institutional constraints on the use of military force.",
      "factual": true,
      "stance": "asserted"
    },
    {
      "id": "a7",
      "pos": 8,
      "text": "Zeev Maoz and Bruce Russett tested the normative and institutional models against each other in a 1993 article in the American Political Science Review.",
      "factual": true,
      "stance": "asserted"
    },
    {
      "id": "a8",
      "pos": 9,
      "text": "Maoz and Russett reported that the normative model received stronger empirical support than the institutional model.",
      "factual": true,
      "stance": "asserted"
    },
    {
      "id": "a9",
      "pos": 10,
      "text": "Maoz and Russett reported that the institutional model outperformed the normative model in their statistical tests.",
      "factual": false,
      "stance": "asserted"
    },
    {
      "id": "a10",
      "pos": 11,
      "text": "Christopher Layne's 1994 article \"Kant or Cant\" in International Security examined four near-war crises between democracies as critical tests.",
      "factual": true,
      "stance": "asserted"
    },
    {
      "id": "a11",
      "pos": 12,
      "text": "Layne's case selection included the 1898 Fashoda crisis between Britain and France.",
      "factual": true,
      "stance": "asserted"
    },
